{{/*
Template draft for `gometagen`.

How to use it:
- Edit this file for your own output format.
- To generate into a file, pass an explicit `-out`:
  gometagen generate -source . -template ./templates/gometagen.tmpl -out ./target/meta.txt
- To generate into stdout, use `-stdout` instead of `-out`.

What is available at the template root:
- `.PackageName`
  Package name used by the built-in Go renderer. Usually not needed in a custom template, but available.
- `.ManifestPath`
  Absolute path to the manifest file that was read.
- `.GeneratedAt`
  Generation time in RFC3339 format.
- `.HashMode`
  Hash mode: `git` or `content`.
- `.HashPoint`
  The effective path used for hashing:
  for `git` this is the repository root or source path,
  for `content` this is the joined list of effective source paths.
- `.HashSource`
  Joined list of effective source paths. Empty when git hash mode is used.
- `.HashSources`
  Effective source paths as a string array.
- `.Manifest`
  Raw manifest values without computed metadata.
- `.Meta`
  Normalized computed values prepared for rendering.

Fields in `.Manifest`:
- `.Manifest.Name`
  Original `name` field from the manifest.
- `.Manifest.Ver`
  Original `ver` field from the manifest.

Fields in `.Meta`:
- `.Meta.Name`
  Project name after normalization for rendering.
- `.Meta.DateUpdate`
  Date in `MM-DD-YYYY` format.
- `.Meta.Hash`
  Final hash value.
- `.Meta.Version`
  Full version string.
- `.Meta.VersionMajor`
  Major version part. Examples: `v1`, `release`.
- `.Meta.VersionMinor`
  Middle numeric version part.
- `.Meta.VersionPatch`
  Lowest numeric version part.

Custom template functions:
- `quote VALUE`
  Escapes a string as a Go string literal.
  Example: `{{ quote .Meta.Version }}`
- `jsonQuote VALUE`
  Escapes a string as a JSON string.
  Example: `{"version": {{ jsonQuote .Meta.Version }}}`
- `yamlInline VALUE`
  Escapes a string as a single-line YAML value.
- `yamlValue VALUE INDENT`
  Escapes a string as a YAML value; for multi-line text it emits a block scalar.
  `INDENT` controls indentation inside the block.

Useful standard `text/template` features:
- `if`, `else`, `with`, `range`
- `printf`, `print`, `println`
- `eq`, `ne`, `lt`, `gt`, `and`, `or`, `not`

Short examples:
- `{{ .Meta.Name }}`
- `{{ if eq .HashMode "git" }}git={{ .Meta.Hash }}{{ end }}`
- `{{ if .HashSource }}hash_source={{ .HashSource }}{{ end }}`
- `{{ range .HashSources }}source={{ . }}{{ end }}`

Minimal working template below.
*/}}
name={{ yamlInline .Meta.Name }}
date_update={{ yamlInline .Meta.DateUpdate }}
hash={{ yamlInline .Meta.Hash }}
version={{ yamlInline .Meta.Version }}
version_major={{ yamlInline .Meta.VersionMajor }}
version_minor={{ .Meta.VersionMinor }}
version_patch={{ .Meta.VersionPatch }}
